The text for -00, for submission before the IETF 127 cutoff (2026-11-02 23:59 UTC).

**Merge with a merge commit, not squash.** That way #13 and #14 show as merged, since their commits are included.

Carries:
- #13: reserved content values;
- #14: discovery without enumeration, distinct prefixes (Alan Frindell's review);
- an editorial sweep (37e6f4b). Clarity and style only, no change to the protocol:
  - abstract and introduction reworded; the introduction lists every parameter;
  - "utilizes" to "uses"; omitted-field and equivalent-namespace sentences clarified; tuple field 0 states its value;
  - clock: the beep and marker fall on whole seconds of capture time;
  - field 13: a clip's views are its synchronized views, if it has them;
  - the two delivery modes as a list; datagram-size and latency sentences reworded; Security Considerations says "publisher", not "server";
  - author email gmarzot@marzresearch.net; Alan Frindell credited for review.

Cited sections checked against draft-ietf-moq-transport-22 (§2.4.2 Namespace Prefix Matching, §8.8 Representing Namespace and Track Names) and draft-frindell-moq-timestamp-00 (§7 Publisher Restarts).

